import{_ as o,o as t,c,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"UXD-001 — The UI accent is blue D, and it replaces every UI teal","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-001-ui-accent-blue-replaces-teal.md","filePath":"uxs/decisions/UXD-001-ui-accent-blue-replaces-teal.md"}'),s={name:"uxs/decisions/UXD-001-ui-accent-blue-replaces-teal.md"};function n(r,e,d,i,l,u){return t(),c("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="uxd-001-—-the-ui-accent-is-blue-d-and-it-replaces-every-ui-teal" tabindex="-1">UXD-001 — The UI accent is blue D, and it replaces every UI teal <a class="header-anchor" href="#uxd-001-—-the-ui-accent-is-blue-d-and-it-replaces-every-ui-teal" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;UXD-001 — The UI accent is blue D, and it replaces every UI teal&quot;">​</a></h1><ul><li><strong>Status</strong>: accepted</li><li><strong>Date</strong>: 2026-11-09 (teal ruled out, proposed for 0.9.9) · 2026-11-11 (blue D chosen and scoped)</li><li><strong>Decider</strong>: the operator. Blue D confirmed &quot;after the sheet&quot; (<code>docs/wip/2026-11-11-ux-feedback-plan.md</code> line 429, commit <code>9dda8b6813f</code> &quot;Q1 blue D confirmed&quot;); scope to every UI teal, and science diagrams and Lab art keep their own colours, &quot;operator 2026-11-11&quot; (same line). Teal ruled out and 0.9.9 named as the redesign arc: operator, 2026-11-09 (operator notes <code>no-cyan</code>, <code>099-redesign</code>; <code>docs/wip/2026-11-09-0.9.9-redesign.md</code> line 3).</li><li><strong>Answers</strong>: X2, G4, Q1; slice A3 (link and accent colour)</li><li><strong>Changes</strong>: <code>src/lib/styles/tokens.css</code> (<code>--color-teal</code>, <code>--color-tier-intro</code>, <code>--color-accent-text</code>); IA §shared-tokens (colour tokens, link tier colours); <code>docs/concept/05_Design_System.md</code> §2.1 to 2.2; AGENTS.md &quot;Design system&quot; colour block; UXS-002 and UXS-003 teal HUD and CAPCOM colours. <em>Rules to be updated to state this and link here (UXS-000 §Next).</em></li></ul><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The operator ruled out cyan and teal for UI states as &quot;out of palette&quot; and &quot;so fake&quot; on 2026-11-09 (operator note <code>no-cyan</code>; <code>docs/wip/2026-11-09-0.9.9-redesign.md</code> line 7). 0.9.8 replaced only the surface-scene states with the muted blue <code>#889fe7</code> (marker hover, the ACTIVE status tone, the start of the route sol ramp, the 3D outline pass).</li><li>The same teal <code>#4ecdc4</code> is the site&#39;s brand accent: about 780 uses in 147 files at 2026-11-09 (operator note <code>099-redesign</code>), about 640 uses in about 123 files in the slice plan (plan line 329, later count). <code>tokens.css</code> holds it as <code>--color-teal</code> and <code>--color-tier-intro</code>.</li><li>The operator&#39;s list asks for it directly: links on credits, colophon and library are &quot;a turquoise colour&quot;; use the muted blue &quot;used in many places; nothing close to glowing&quot; (X2); the muted blue in the gallery footer is &quot;a better choice for coloured text than the turquoise elsewhere&quot; (G4). The operator also said to merge the teal redesign into the feedback list (plan line 5).</li></ul><h2 id="options" tabindex="-1">Options <a class="header-anchor" href="#options" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Options&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Q1 offered two blues (plan line 404): <code>#889fe7</code> (status chips, rings) or <code>#7fb0e0</code> (gallery, programs), and asked whether the change covers links only or every UI teal. The operator chose &quot;blue D&quot;, <code>#5070ff</code>, after seeing a colour sheet. The sheet is not in the repository; what blues A to C and the others were is not recorded in the sources.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Decision&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The UI accent colour is <strong>blue D, <code>#5070ff</code></strong>, which is today&#39;s global link colour (<code>--color-accent-text</code>). It replaces <strong>every UI teal</strong>: links, HUD chips, home glyphs and panels. There is no cyan or teal anywhere in the UI.</p><p><strong>The muted blue <code>#889fe7</code> stays alongside D</strong>: D (<code>#5070ff</code>) for links and accents, <code>#889fe7</code> for annotation rings, hover and status states (operator go, 2026-11-11, <code>docs/wip/2026-11-11-ux-feedback-plan.md</code>, line starting &quot;- Operator go, 2026-11-11 (session&quot;, line 460).</p><p><strong>Science diagrams and Lab art keep their own colours</strong> (the <code>/science</code> diagram style and the Lab goal art are unaffected; operator 2026-11-09 and 2026-11-11). This is &quot;for now&quot;: the operator listed &quot;review whether they should also move to the new palette once the UI blue is in place&quot; as an end-of-work check (plan lines 462–465).</p><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Consequences&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Slice A3 replaces teal in UI files by the token (grep: no teal in UI files outside an allow-list) and ends with shots of credits, colophon, library, posters, science and the explore HUD (plan line 329).</li><li>Teal that is science data and not UI is outside the rule; the redesign note lists the candidates (Moon tidal-lock overlay, Earth limb glow, microgravity axes, Lab canvases, fly velocity arrows, universe scenes, <code>epoch-bands</code>) and says which stay (<code>docs/wip/2026-11-09-0.9.9-redesign.md</code> lines 18–22).</li><li>The surface scenes keep <code>#889fe7</code> (<code>HOVER_BLUE</code>, <code>src/lib/surface-scene/surface-markers.ts</code> line 45) for rings, hover and status states, next to D (plan line 460).</li><li>The status tones ACTIVE <code>#889fe7</code> and PLANNED <code>#7b9cff</code> are near-identical; the redesign note says to &quot;revisit with the new palette&quot; (lines 23–25). Open.</li></ul><h2 id="implementation-slice-a3-2026-11-12" tabindex="-1">Implementation (slice A3, 2026-11-12) <a class="header-anchor" href="#implementation-slice-a3-2026-11-12" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Implementation (slice A3, 2026-11-12)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Operator answers on the A3 brief (plan line &quot;- A3 accent colour (operator 2026-11-12&quot;):</p><ol><li><code>--color-accent</code> is <code>#5070ff</code>, the one UI accent; <code>#4466ff</code> is retired (51 hex and 92 rgba uses became tokens); <code>--color-accent-text</code> stays as an alias for one release; <code>--color-teal</code> is removed.</li><li>Link tiers: intro <code>#889fe7</code> (<code>--color-state</code>), core blue D, deep gold. The green &quot;ok&quot; <code>#2dd4a8</code> is its own <code>--color-ok</code> token. There is no <code>--color-tier-intro</code>.</li><li>Data colours stay and carry <code>a3-keep: &lt;why&gt;</code>: orbit regimes, agency and nation identity, era bands, universe star colours, microgravity and magnetic axes, the /plan heat map (and its three locale prose keys, unchanged). They go to the end-of-work palette review.</li><li>Lab chrome (Notebook, Card, <code>routes/lab</code>) moves to D; Lab canvases and figures keep theirs.</li></ol><p>Final token names (<code>src/lib/styles/tokens.css</code>): <code>--color-accent</code>, <code>--color-accent-text</code> (alias), <code>--color-accent-hover</code> <code>#8aa0ff</code>, <code>--color-accent-soft</code> / <code>-edge</code> / <code>-strong</code> (<code>rgba(80, 112, 255, 0.12 / 0.35 / 0.7)</code>), <code>--color-state</code> <code>#889fe7</code>, <code>--color-focus</code> <code>#8aa0ff</code>, <code>--color-ok</code> <code>#4ade80</code> (was <code>#2dd4a8</code>, hue 163, moved to a clear green 2026-11-12 so it is never read as teal). Other alphas are <code>color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-accent) N%, transparent)</code>. <code>#7fb0e0</code> (page-section <code>.k</code> field labels, entity pages, gallery and programs chips) folded into <code>--color-state</code>.</p><p>/fly HUD (held in A3, decided 2026-11-12 after the four-candidate sheets: cyan, blue D, neutral white, cockpit green): blue D, for consistency with the rest of the site. The six fly files (<code>routes/fly/+page.svelte</code>, <code>CoastScene</code>, <code>DescentScene</code>, <code>LaunchTelemetry</code>, <code>LaunchScene</code>, <code>AscentLosses</code>) carry no colour literals for the HUD: cyan <code>#7fd4ff</code> became <code>--color-state</code>, <code>#8fbfe0</code> / <code>#6ea6cc</code> <code>--color-accent-hover</code>, the coast scrubber <code>#6fb7ff</code> <code>--color-accent</code>, their alphas <code>color-mix</code>. Known trade: labels over the bright launch sky read lower than cyan did.</p><p>Contrast rule: D is 4.96:1 on the page and the HUD, 4.37 on a 7 % lifted card, 3.84 on a 12 % lift. Text under 14 px bold / 18 px on a lifted surface uses <code>--color-state</code> (6.1:1 or better); a solid D fill takes dark text <code>#04040c</code> (4.96:1), not white (4.12:1).</p><h2 id="verification" tabindex="-1">Verification <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>A3 check script (brief section 10): <code>A3-CHECK violations: 0</code>, retired token references 0.</li><li><code>src/lib/styles/tokens.test.ts</code> asserts the token values and that no teal token exists.</li><li><code>tests/e2e/accent-colour.spec.ts</code> reads computed colours on every named screen and every route family (no teal hue) and checks accent text contrast against its backdrop.</li></ul>',20)])])}const f=o(s,[["render",n]]);export{p as __pageData,f as default};
